{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-04_exhibit991ecpgq32026earnin.htm, sha256 a7dd935c71835bfdb61e428876afbcf4a7b03e56aecc98b0be19d496937a3ba3.\nEX-99.1 2 exhibit991ecpgq32026earnin.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1\nEncore Capital Group Announces Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results\n\u2022Favorable purchasing conditions continue in U.S. market \u2022Global portfolio purchases of $390 million, including $310 million in U.S. \u2022Global collections up 14% to record $754 million \u2022Earnings per share up 76% to $5.57\nSAN DIEGO, November 4, 2026 -- Encore Capital Group, Inc. (NASDAQ: ECPG), an international specialty finance company, today reported consolidated financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026. \u201cEncore delivered an exceptional third quarter, both financially and operationally, highlighted by strong portfolio purchasing and record global collections,\u201d said Ashish Masih, President and Chief Executive Officer. \u201cThird quarter global portfolio purchases were $390 million and global collections were a record $754 million, up 14% compared to a year ago. This collections performance helped drive GAAP net income in the third quarter of $124 million or $5.57 per share, up 76% compared to $3.17 per share a year ago.\u201d\n\u201cMCM, our U.S. business, continues to set the pace. The U.S. market remains highly attractive for us, supported by continued robust portfolio supply, and we are capitalizing on that opportunity with discipline and conviction. MCM purchased $310 million of portfolios in the third quarter and delivered record collections of $589 million, up 17% compared to the third quarter a year ago. This exceptional collections performance is the result of strong execution and continued significant portfolio purchasing as well as the deployment of new technologies, enhanced digital capabilities and continued operational innovation.\u201d \u201cIn Europe, our Cabot business delivered a solid third quarter. Portfolio purchases were $80 million while collections of $164 million were up 2% compared to the third quarter last year.\u201d\n\u201cGiven the strength and momentum of our business, we are raising our full-year 2026 guidance. We now anticipate global portfolio purchases to be in a range between $1.50 billion and $1.55 billion, and global collections to be in a range between $2.90 billion and $2.95 billion, reflecting year-over-year growth of 12-14%. Additionally, we now expect our EPS in 2026 to be in a range between $15.50 and $16.00 per share, an increase of over 40% compared to 2025. As always, we remain committed to the critical role we play in the consumer credit ecosystem and to helping consumers restore their financial health,\u201d said Masih.\nIn the third quarter, the company repurchased approximately $27 million of its shares of common stock, bringing total repurchases through the first nine months of 2026 to approximately $73 million.\nEncore Capital Group, Inc. Page 2\nFinancial Highlights for the Third Quarter of 2026:\nThree Months Ended September 30,\n"}
